                        <note type="MLGB3_generalNotes">B.L. Arundel 36, Cotton Vesp. B.xi fols.
                           84–125, 125* and Royal 13 A.xxi fols. 151–192 formed one volume; see A.
                           G. Watson, The Manuscripts of Henry Savile of Banke (1969), pp.
                           74–77.</note>
                        <note type="MLGB3_generalNotes">Leaves numbered 58–100 in s. xvi, in
                           continuation of the numbering 1–57 in Arundel 36 q. v. Fols. 84–86 are
                           the last three leaves of a quire, presumably the same quire as that from
                           which Arundel 36, fols. 53–57 come. Text goes straight on from Arundel
                           36 fol. 57v and in the same hand.</note>
